      "empirical": false,
      "source": "manuscript/main_body.md",
      "section": "4.2. Measurement and inference",
      "caption": "**Table 1. Hypotheses and benchmark comparison.**",
      "columns": [
        "Hypothesis or comparison",
        "Question"
      ],
      "rows": [
        [
          "**H1. Placement power**",
          "Does the mean conditional received share exceed 50% for B on the three-node line, the node class containing B and D on the five-node line, and the hub of each star? H1 requires this in all four networks."
        ],
        [
          "**H2. Benchmark fit**",
          "Which theoretical reference best matches observed mean earnings across node classes: the equal-split earnings reference, Myerson value, position value or the selected balanced outcome? H2 ranks prediction errors; it is not a significance test. Hence, it does not produce a hypothesis-test p-value."
        ],
        [
          "**H3. Star dose-response**",
          "Is there a positive linear trend in the hub's mean conditional received share as the number of leaves increases from two to four? The three-node line is treated as a two-leaf star, alongside the three- and four-leaf stars."
        ],
        [
          "**H4. End-agent earnings**",
          "Do agents at the ends of the four-node line earn more, on average, than agents at the ends of the five-node line?"
        ],
        [
          "**H5. Network knowledge**",
          "Does the mean power-use index differ between the full-map and own-links knowledge settings across the six eligible networks?"
        ]
      ],
      "source_sha256": "706b49686226164528e49fad977b7652d379a29c2dfc2ce75ded0cd78a807636"
    },
